GT patch 0033: render targets and the internal scale.
- A render target stands for its VRAM only while the GE draws into it: a texture reads a target only if a draw
  into it was recorded within the last 60 frames (one second). GT rendered a menu label into VRAM, left the menu
  and loaded the kerbs' texture over those bytes with the CPU (which the backend never sees): the stale target
  drew "Single Player" on the kerbs.
- Window mode keeps the internal scale under a GPU budget (Rendering.GpuBudgetMs, default 10 ms, 0 = off):
  measured with the frame timestamps, one whole scale down while the GPU needs more per frame, one up when the
  next scale would fit well inside and the last change is 6 s old (budget_scale_cap), never past what the
  window needs.

